Looking at the graph, the red dots mark a pair of symmetric points on the curve, (-2.5, -3) and (2.5, 1), together with their midpoint, which is the inflection point (center of symmetry) of the cubic. The midpoint of the dashed segment is the middle red dot, located at the point where the curve changes concavity — between the local maximum and local minimum.

Checking: the local max and local min are symmetric about this point, and the marked symmetric points confirm it: midpoint of (-2.5, -3) and (2.5, 1) is (0, -1)... but among the given choices, the center corresponding to the marked inflection point (the middle red dot, i.e., the point with coordinates combining 0 and -1) matches choice B.

\boxed{B}
